      "response": "\nOrchestra Pit, in Midair\nYou are almost at the bottom of the pit. Now that impact is so imminent, you \nalmost wish you could keep on falling.\n\nRob the Guard adjusts his spectacles. \"And should he, in that time, learn to \nplay better, it shall not matter, since there is no way back out of the Pit. \nThis I hereby put to paper as my word is the law when the law is my word, when \nit is heard. Indeed. Thus I spake. Er, spoke. Alright, scribe, stop your \ndictating now.\" Finishing, Rob rolls up the scroll and puts it away.\n\nWith a loud SHLURP, you land in the mud at the bottom of the pit...\n\nPit Bottom\nThe pit is about twenty yards in diameter and run-off from the sides drains \ninto a large mud puddle in the center of floor. The air is thick with the odour \nof mud and mildew.\n\nYou stretch and do a quick check, thankfully finding that you're still whole.\n\nJim grimaces and sucks his tooth. \"Ouch! That had to sting...\" He cups his \nmouth and shouts down to you, \"You're lucky, old pal! A few people have been \nknown to break all of their limbs with that drop!\" He elbows Rob and snickers. \n\"But then, it wouldn't be much of an experience if he up and died so quickly, \neh?\" Rob nods. \"Indeed...\"\n\nBy some trick of acoustics, you can still hear the guards' banter quite clearly.\n\n>",
